<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="10">
<name>Body &amp; Electrical</name>
<section id="1002S_S000E" variety="S000E">
<name>Vehicle Surroundings Monitor</name>
<ttl id="1002S_S000E_742B9_T003J" variety="T003J">
<name>Intelligent Parking Assist System</name>
<para id="RM0000002O201AX" category="D" type-id="3001B" name-id="672DU-00" from="200612" to="200912">
<name>How to Proceed with Troubleshooting</name>
<subpara id="RM0000002O201AX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___00001J000000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<descript-diag>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Vehicle brought to workshop</testtitle>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Customer Problem Analysis and Symptom Check</testtitle>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Customer Problem Analysis and Symptom Check (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM00000045U00ZX"/>)</ptxt>
</atten4>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Basic Inspection</testtitle>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Basic Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the battery voltage.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Standard</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>11 to 14 V (IG OFF)</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Inspect areas that can be checked visually, such as blown fuses, open or short circuits in the wire harness and poor connector connections.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>CAN Communication System Check</testtitle>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), select "Diagnosis" → "CAN Bus Diagnosis" → "CAN Bus Connected ECU Check" to display the connected ECU check screen, and check all ECUs and sensors connected to CAN communication. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000001R4W009X"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.30in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No Abnormality</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Abnormal</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to CAN Communication System (see <xref label="Seep03" href="RM0000005S001MX"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Check DTC</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check Diagnostic Trouble Code (see <xref label="Seep04" href="RM000000OCQ007X"/>)</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Some DTCs are output even when there is no malfunction if the inspection is performed with the IG ON, so always perform the check with the engine running.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<test2>
<ptxt>Record the DTCs.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Perform inspection and repair according to the instructions in the Diagnostic Trouble Code Chart.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Clear DTC</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Recheck DTC</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.30in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No Screen Display</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No code (symptom can be confirmed and reproduced)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No code (symptom cannot be confirmed and reproduced)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Code output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to Symptom Simulation (see <xref label="Seep05" href="RM000000ABY03DX"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result>C</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to step 10</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Service Inspection (AVC-LAN Connection Check and AVC-LAN DTC Check)</testtitle>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>For details of the service inspection procedure, refer to <xref label="Seep07" href="RM0000002O8017X"/></ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<test1>
<ptxt>Service Inspection (AVC-LAN Connection Check)</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>On the service inspection screen, check that all connected devices are displayed.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.10in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Part Name</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Device Name</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Navigation Receiver Assembly</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>AVN</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Television Camera Controller</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>CAMERA-C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Service Inspection (Individual Diagnosis Check)</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Some DTCs are output even when there is no malfunction if the inspection is performed with the IG ON, so always perform the check with the engine running.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<test2>
<ptxt>Record the DTCs.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Perform inspection and repair according to the instructions in the Diagnostic Trouble Code Chart.</ptxt>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.99in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.14in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Device Name</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Reference</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>AVN</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep09" href="RM0000002RS03EX"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>CAMERA-C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>
<xref label="Seep10" href="RM0000002O401AX"/>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Clear DTC</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Recheck DTC</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Based on the recorded DTCs, reproduce the problem symptom and check whether the DTCs are output again.</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.30in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No code, symptom can be confirmed and reproduced</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>No code, symptom cannot be confirmed and reproduced</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Code output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>All connected devices other than AVN are displayed as "Not Connected"</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>All connected devices other than AVN are not displayed</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>D</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to Symptom Simulation (see <xref label="Seep11" href="RM000000ABY03DX"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result>C</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to step 10</action-ci-right>
<result>D</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to HDD Navigation System - Troubleshooting Flowchart AVC-LAN Malfunction (see <xref label="Seep13" href="RM0000007EM02GX"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Symptom Check</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check whether the same symptom occurs with the HDD navigation system.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.30in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Same symptom does not occur</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Same symptom occurs</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to HDD Navigation System - Problem Symptoms Table (see <xref label="Seep15" href="RM0000008WW01OX"/>)</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>List by Symptom</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>Problem Symptoms Table (see <xref label="Seep16" href="RM0000002O7016X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.30in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.83in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Not listed in List by Symptom</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Corresponds to List by Symptom [When Replacing Navigation Receiver Assembly]</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Corresponds to List by Symptom [When Replacing Devices Other Than Above]</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<results>
<result>B</result>
<action-ci-right>Go to step 10</action-ci-right>
<result-ci-down>A</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Perform troubleshooting using the following methods based on the problem symptom</testtitle>
<test1>
<ptxt>ECU Data Monitor/Active Test (see <xref label="Seep17" href="RM000000OAS007X"/>)</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>ECU Data Monitor (TaSCAN)</ptxt>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Terminals of ECU (see <xref label="Seep18" href="RM0000002O6018X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Adjust, Repair or Replace</testtitle>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Work after Replacement</testtitle>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When the battery terminal is disconnected, perform the setting operations required when the battery terminal is removed and installed. (see <xref label="Seep19" href="RM000001LYW00PX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Depending on the parts replaced or the work performed during vehicle inspection and maintenance, registration and setting operations for other systems as well as the intelligent parking assist system may be necessary. (see <xref label="Seep20" href="RM00000304S000X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When replacing the navigation receiver assembly on a vehicle not subscribed to the G-BOOK service, perform the vehicle linking setting.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When replacing the navigation receiver assembly on a vehicle subscribed to the G-BOOK service, perform the vehicle linking setting, then perform the G-BOOK use resumption operation and HELPNET service start operation.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the navigation receiver assembly is replaced while a purchased G-SOUND unlimited license exists, perform G-SOUND license recovery.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
<descript-testgroup>
<testtitle>Confirmation Test</testtitle>
<results>
<result-ci-down>NEXT</result-ci-down>
<action-ci-fin>END</action-ci-fin>
</results>
</descript-testgroup>
</descript-diag>
</content5>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
</tmc-service-inc>